The <strong>2019</strong> <strong>Acura MDX</strong> is a midsize luxury SUV that offers seating for up to seven passengers. It comes standard with a 3.5-liter V6 engine that produces 290 horsepower and 267 lb-ft of torque. The MDX comes standard with a nine-speed automatic transmission and front-wheel drive. All-wheel drive is available.

The MDX is available in three trim levels: Standard, Technology, and Advance. Standard features include 18-inch alloy wheels, LED headlights, a power liftgate, a sunroof, tri-zone automatic climate control, leather upholstery, heated front seats, a power-adjustable steering wheel, driver memory settings, a dual-screen infotainment system, Apple CarPlay and Android Auto, and an eight-speaker sound system.

The Technology package adds 20-inch wheels, rain-sensing wipers, blind-spot monitoring, rear cross-traffic alert, navigation, a 10-speaker ELS sound system, and a rear-seat entertainment system.

The Advance package adds 20-inch wheels, a surround-view camera system, front and rear parking sensors, ventilated front seats, heated second-row seats, a heated steering wheel, and a 14-speaker ELS sound system.

The MDX is a great choice for families who need a spacious and comfortable SUV. It offers a smooth ride, a quiet cabin, and a long list of standard features. The MDX is also available with a variety of advanced safety features,